<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mortagne-au-Perche</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mortagne-au-Perche is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orne-river">Orne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Normandy, historic capital of the Perche. Its lords, who also held Nogent, became counts of Perche in the 11th century and ruled the county until their line ended in 1226. The town is known for its black pudding and for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/percheron">Percheron</a> horses bred in the surrounding hills.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mortagne-au-perche.jpg" alt="Mortagne-au-Perche" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alonso de Mendoza · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayuntamiento_de_Mortagne-au-Perche,_Normand%C3%ADa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
